From 3a31d2a8e726409d2d9ebf149bc116e9e014915a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 14:32:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Execution policies for the material properties of the
 generic-parallel interface

- Version 2 of the functions of the material properties generated by the
  generic-parallel interface of TFEL: a last argument gives the execution
  options (queue, preservation of the stack size), with the same meaning
  for all the backends. `mgis_mp_ExecutionOptions` is a copy of the
  structure of TFEL.
- `evaluate(e, values, mp, inputs[, location, bounds_policy])` evaluates a
  material property on the queue of the given execution policy, as
  `integrate(policy, ...)` for behaviours. The overload without execution
  policy uses the default queue of the backend.
- `BatchExecutionPolicy` moves to the `mgis` namespace
  (`MGIS/BatchExecutionPolicy.hxx`): it is shared by behaviours, models and
  material properties.
- The statuses reporting invalid arguments and errors of the backend (-5,
  -6, -7) are raised as exceptions, as for behaviours: they are never
  reported as a failure of the evaluation.
